WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.820
Give a PC12 cell the growth factor EGF, and it divides.

2
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:15.960
Give the same cell NGF, and it stops dividing and grows long, nerve-like fibres.

3
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:23.760
Both signals run through the same four proteins: Ras, Raf, MEK and ERK.

4
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.040
How can one chain of enzymes carry two instructions?

5
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.100
At the membrane, SOS loads Ras with GTP, and Ras is on.

6
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:39.240
Ras is not a kinase, so it works by contact.

7
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.480
Active Ras catches Raf, a kinase that floats in the cytosol, folded shut.

8
00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.040
Binding brings Raf to the membrane and helps pull it open.

9
00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:56.580
Then two Raf molecules pair, side by side, and pairing is needed for normal

10
00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.580
activation.

11
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.980
Active Raf adds phosphates to the next kinase, MEK, on two serines.

12
00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.900
MEK then does something unusual.

13
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:14.940
It adds a phosphate to a threonine and another to a tyrosine, one residue apart, on

14
00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.240
ERK. ERK needs both.

15
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.500
Take either one off, and ERK goes quiet.

16
00:01:22.283 --> 00:01:28.223
Negative feedback sets how long the signal lasts, and ERK supplies its own.

17
00:01:29.183 --> 00:01:35.123
Active ERK phosphorylates proteins above it in the chain, among them SOS and Raf,

18
00:01:35.603 --> 00:01:36.823
and that weakens them.

19
00:01:37.603 --> 00:01:43.563
It also turns on genes for phosphatases, enzymes that take both phosphates back off

20
00:01:43.563 --> 00:01:49.003
ERK. That second kind of feedback is slower, because a protein has to be made.

21
00:01:51.483 --> 00:01:57.563
Different stimuli leave the pathway on for different lengths of time before feedback

22
00:01:57.563 --> 00:01:58.683
closes the window.

23
00:01:59.783 --> 00:02:06.803
In a PC12 cell, ERK activity after EGF rises and falls back within about an hour.

24
00:02:07.623 --> 00:02:11.843
After NGF, it climbs to a plateau that lasts for hours.

25
00:02:13.023 --> 00:02:18.343
In 1995, Christopher Marshall proposed that this difference is itself the

26
00:02:18.343 --> 00:02:23.323
instruction. A brief signal goes with division, and a sustained one with

27
00:02:23.323 --> 00:02:24.323
differentiation.

28
00:02:24.967 --> 00:02:29.887
Now force MEK on for good, with no growth factor at all.

29
00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:36.587
ERK then stays on without end, which the cell cannot tell apart from a long NGF

30
00:02:36.587 --> 00:02:44.687
signal. In 1994, Cowley and Marshall did this, and PC12 cells grew fibres with no

31
00:02:44.687 --> 00:02:51.967
NGF. One caution: this rule comes from one cell line, and how widely it holds is an

32
00:02:51.967 --> 00:03:00.047
open question. So keep this rule: in a PC12 cell, how long ERK stays on carries the instruction.
